    "body": "The existing fork/org drift story has five criteria but the current project CLI validates only local map/project/lineage data and ignores the later `--remote` flag. This planning refinement preserves the original Incoming/P2/two-point card and proposes the complete portable ancestry law, isolated Git observation adapter, actual CLI failure proof and externally owned protected post-promotion sync seam.\n\nThe proposal distinguishes workspace `orgTip → forkMain` from canonical promotion's `orgTip → receipt-bound qualified feature X`. A moving fork tip cannot substitute for X; post-sync proof binds immutable promotion M and refreshed org/fork tips. Witnessed positive ancestry and complete-negative drift remain distinct from shallow/unavailable unknown evidence.\n\nRefs [original merged planning #122](https://github.com/open-hax/foresight/pull/122) and existing UUID `fork-org-drift-check`. This development plan stacks on pending personal [synchronization PR #3](https://github.com/riatzukiza/foresight/pull/3); historical approvals and source availability do not qualify this proposal. Eta-mu-owned promotion/protected-sync, existing map admission, parent qualification, whole-story sizing/review and lawful Rheos Ready remain explicit holds. No implementation, controller, native transition, activation or excluded skill-catalog change is included.\n\nValidation: all 528 other inherited entries and three full byte prefixes are exact; all 68 published lossless transport containers verify. Actual source-built ef3 Rheos reads unchanged authoritative EDN before/after, all 66 fixture inputs in each remain unchanged, and drift stays Incoming/P2/2. Current CI NBB 1.4.207 / Node 22.20.0: project 14 tests / 176 assertions and workspace 24 tests / 120 assertions pass; map/project validate exits 0; root lint has 0 errors / 0 warnings. Expected mocked workspace refusal diagnostics and older NBB 1.3.204 streams are retained distinctly.\n\nThe actual immutable root consumer accepts full head (200 receipts / one appended), and owning Receipt River 154440 accepts the one required-repo compatibility decision row. The 199 historical rows remain byte-exact; 107 current-owner RR refusals are explicitly retained, not repaired or promoted to a blanket pass. Portable canonical reflection append/readback, complete-store isolation, clean source and full base-to-head hygiene are verified. Local peer evidence and passing unchanged baselines do not provide native review/cohort credit. Automatic merge remains off; current planning is unqualified.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Documentation**\n  - Added a planning proposal that clarifies how fork and upstream drift should be assessed, including how uncertain or incomplete evidence should be handled.\n  - Documented proposed verification criteria, ownership boundaries, outstanding decisions, and implementation holds.\n- **Verification**\n  - Recorded baseline validation, test, and lint results. Project validation, project tests, and lint passed; workspace tests passed with some checks unavailable.\n  - Added evidence records confirming planning inputs remained unchanged and no implementation or operational state change occurred.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
